  ],
  "note": "From the official 'Keyboard shortcuts for Microsoft Teams' Microsoft Support article (Windows and MacOS tabs), current as of 2026-09. Only the Desktop-app column was used for 'windows' and the Mac-app column for 'mac'; the article's separate Web-app columns were skipped since this catalog entry matches only the installed desktop app, not the browser. Skipped as not expressible: 'Add reaction' style emoji-picker shortcuts are not listed with fixed chords in this article. The app-bar and chat-header shortcuts (Ctrl/Cmd/Alt+1-9) assume the default app-bar order, per the article's own note; a reordered app bar changes what each number opens. 'Show help' (Calendar) uses the literal '?' character, written here as its US-layout chord Shift+/. Deduplicated several rows that the source article itself lists twice with identical Desktop/Mac chords under slightly different names: 'Go previous/next time period' vs 'Go to the previous/next time period' (Windows), 'Open an event'/'Delete an event' vs 'Open/Delete the selected item', 'Save an appointment' vs 'Save or send meeting request', 'Discard draft' vs 'Close', and Mac's 'Switch the view to include today' vs 'Go to today', and Mac's 'In Day/Week/Month view, move to previous/next...' vs 'Go to the previous/next time period'. Skipped the Windows-only 'Switch to Day view / full Week view / Month view / Work week view / three-day view / List view' block entirely: it directly contradicts the article's own 'Open Day/Week/Month view' shortcuts listed just above it (e.g. both 'Switch to full Week view' and 'Switch to Work week view' are given as Ctrl+Alt+2, and Alt+3 is separately claimed by 'Open Week view', 'Show 3 days in the calendar', and 'Switch to three-day view'), so no single trustworthy chord could be recorded for it. A few chords collide across different contexts exactly as the source documents them (e.g. mac 'Pin a window on top' and 'Move focus to toast' are both Shift+Cmd+T; mac 'Accept screen share' and 'Accept video call' are both Shift+Cmd+V) — kept as documented since the names and contexts differ. 'Mark all messages as read', 'Edit last sent/selected message', 'See all items you are mentioned in', 'Move focus to Chat options', 'Toggle live captions', 'Create a new appointment or calendar item', and the two calendar 'Navigate to the previous/next pane' shortcuts are Mac-only additions with no Windows equivalent in this article; 'Insert block quote' and most of the day/week/month Calendar navigation shortcuts are Windows-only with no Mac equivalent listed.",
